/FB 15 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 742 Tm
(6. Row-Level Security Rules) Tj
/FR 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 720 Tm
(MongoDB does not automatically enforce row-level security like some SQL databases. In) Tj
/FR 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 706 Tm
(Edgecipline, row-level security must be enforced in the application layer.) Tj
/FR 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 692 Tm
(Plain English rule:) Tj
/FR 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 76 678 Tm
(Every query for user-owned data must include the logged-in user's ID.) Tj
/FB 12 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 662 Tm
(Global Rule) Tj
/FR 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 645 Tm
(If a collection has a user, userId, or owner field, every normal user request must be) Tj
/FR 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 631 Tm
(filtered by that owner field.) Tj
/FR 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 617 Tm
(Examples:) Tj
/FR 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 603 Tm
(- A user requesting trades must only query trades where trade.user = currentUser.id.) Tj
/FR 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 589 Tm
(- A user requesting reports must only query reports where report.user =) Tj
/FR 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 575 Tm
(  currentUser.id.) Tj
/FR 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 561 Tm
(- A user requesting notification history must only query records where) Tj
/FR 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 547 Tm
(  notification.user = currentUser.id.) Tj
/FB 12 Tf
